speechtext:
1.	At present there are no Canadian delegates, representatives or other personnel in Washington in connection with the discussions on international currency stabilization. During April 21 to 26, as a result of an invitation from the secretary of the United States treasury, four Canadian Government officials participated in an informal discussion of the proposal for a United and Associated Nations Stabilization Fund with experts of the United States treasury. These discussions were purely exploratory and non-committal.
2.	Dr. W. A. Mackintosh, special assistant to the deputy minister of finance;
Mr. L. Rasminsky, assistant to the chairman, foreign exchange control board;
Mr. A. F. W. Plumptre, financial attache, Canadian legation, Washington;
Mr. J. J. Deutsch, special wartime assistant, Department of External Affairs.
3.	Each of these persons is a Canadian citizen.
4.	Each of the persons mentioned in 2 is a British subject by birth.
5.	Each of the persons mentioned in 2 was born in Canada.
